dding:7px 10px;margin:4px 5px 0 0;color:#cbd3e0;font-size:13px}.source{font-size:13px;color:#8f99aa}.source a{color:#fff}</style></head><body><main class="wrap"><header class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Reddott Films · <?=esc($book['topic'])?></div><h1><?=esc($book['headline'])?></h1><p class="muted">Published <?=esc(substr($published,0,10))?> · Source-grounded editorial article<?php if($transcript):?> with available captions<?php endif;?>.</p><?php foreach($book['keywords'] as $k):?><span class="tag"><?=esc($k)?></span><?php endforeach;?></header><article class="card article"><?php if($thumb):?><img src="<?=esc($thumb)?>" alt="<?=esc($title)?>" style="width:100%;border-radius:14px;display:block;margin-bottom:20px" loading="eager"><?php endif;?><div class="video"><iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/<?=esc($id)?>" title="<?=esc($title)?>" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe></div><p><?=$book['intro']?></p><p><strong>Source context:</strong> <?=esc($book['sourceSummary'])?></p><?php foreach($book['sections'] as $section):?><h2><?=esc($section[0])?></h2><p><?=esc($section[1])?></p><?php endforeach;?><?php if($description):?><h2>What the creator published</h2><p><?=nl2br(esc($description))?></p><?php endif;?><h2>Search intent: useful questions around this topic</h2><p>This page is organised around <strong><?=esc($book['subject'])?></strong> so a reader can understand the subject, identify relevant concepts and know what to verify in the original source. Keywords are used as descriptors rather than repeated mechanically.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><?php foreach($book['faq'] as $q=>$a):?><h3><?=esc($q)?></h3><p><?=esc($a)?></p><?php endforeach;?><p><a class="btn" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=<?=rawurlencode($id)?>" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch the original on YouTube</a></p></article><aside class="card source"><strong>Editorial standard:</strong> Title, published description and available YouTube captions are treated as source material. General explanations are clearly contextual. Unsupported facts, statistics, quotes and unseen-scene claims are not invented. Articles become indexable only when sufficient source material exists; otherwise they remain noindex for editorial review.<br><br><a href="/Reddott-films/blogs/">← Reddott Films Blog</a> · <a href="/privacy-policy.php">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms.php">Terms</a></aside></main></body></html>
